window.ORACLE_BRIEFING = {"date":"2026-10-26","markdown":"# ORACLE Briefing — Monday, October 26, 2026\n\n**Bottom line:** Oil closed at its highest price since April (Brent $116.72) as Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia widened the Gulf conflict, and stocks fell; the Fed decides Wednesday and the midterms are eight days away.\n\n**Volatility:** V = 0.52 → Path Gamma (tense but holding, ▲ from 0.48) · closest in level: Nov 1979 Iran hostage crisis and stagflation, Jan 2021 Capitol attack · closest in kind: Jan 1979 Winter of Discontent, Aug 2011 debt-ceiling showdown · shock watch 41% for the next 7 days (record: 0 graded, not yet scored)\n\n## 🗣️ In plain English\nOil jumped to about $117 a barrel on Friday, the highest since April, after Yemen's Houthi fighters attacked Saudi Arabia's oil sites, and stocks slipped (the S&P 500 ended at 7,624, below the 7,700 mark we asked about, so that forecast was wrong-way for a \"yes\"). Oil eased a little on Monday on hopes the Iran fighting may calm down, but a US-Iran deal to reopen Gulf shipping by mid-November still looks unlikely (14%). The Federal Reserve meets Wednesday and is more likely to hold rates (about 80%) than raise them. Oil staying above $100 by Oct 30 looks very likely (85%), and October inflation coming in at 3.7% or higher is a bit more likely than not (61%). Democrats are still very likely to win the House (87%); the Senate is close to a coin flip (52%). Watch this week for the Fed on Wednesday, the growth report on Thursday, and Justice Department moves around the election. Things are about 0.52 out of 1: tense but holding, about as shaky as November 1979, when the Iran hostage crisis and high prices rattled the country. The chance of a big shock this week is about 41%.\n\n## ⚡ Top moves\n- Brent above $100 on Oct 30 — **85%** (▲ 11 pts) — Brent settled $116.72 on Oct 23; ~$115 Oct 26.\n- S&P 500 above 7,800 on Oct 30 — **21%** (▼ 8 pts) — index closed 7,623.68 Oct 23; needs +2.3% in a week.\n- Oct CPI ≥ 3.7% y/y — **61%** (▲ 5 pts) — oil +6% on the week; gasoline likely higher in October.\n- Fed hike Oct 28 — **20%** (▼ 3 pts) — futures reportedly ~82% hold (Oct 20); market 15%.\n- Iran shipping deal by Nov 14 — **14%** (unchanged) — oil dip on easing hopes, but no verified talks.\n\n## 🧱 Systems\n- Inflation: pressure 7.4 vs friction 5.9 → tipping (gauge 71%, sandbox 75%) — pressure +0.3 on oil at a six-month high. The 15-pt gap to P-0015 (61%) is intentional: the system tips on a broader price slide than one CPI print.\n- Growth: 5.0 vs 7.0 → strained (gauge 23%, sandbox 26%) — pressure +0.4 for the oil shock and Dow's 1.2% drop.\n- Hormuz: 3.8 vs 6.7 → holding (15%, sandbox 20%) — momentum flag left as is: this system tips only on a shipping deal, and the Monday oil dip rests on hopes, not verified talks.\n- House 87% / Senate 52% unchanged; the 9th Circuit looked skeptical of DOJ's bid to set aside 20,000 California ballots (courts containing it), while DOJ escalation before the election is a pressure on trust.\n\n## 🔀 Catalyst watch\n- Oct 28 Fed decision: IF hold (60% in registry; ORACLE hike odds 20%) → growth pressure eases slightly; IF hike → stocks and growth take a hit. Note: registry branch odds (40/60) lag ORACLE's 20% hike number.\n- Oct 29 Q3 GDP: IF ≥1% (70%) → growth holds; IF weak → stagflation worries rise.\n- Nov 3 Midterms: IF Democrats win the House (87%) → biggest shift in the House system.\n\n## ✅ Report card\n- Resolved: S&P 500 above 7,700 on Oct 23 → NO (closed 7,623.68). ORACLE 42% (✓, Brier 0.176); closer engine: OMEN (0.123 vs CLIO 0.250). Economy weights now CLIO 0.45 / OMEN 0.55.\n- Running: ORACLE 0.108 · CLIO 0.153 · OMEN 0.076 · Sandbox n/a · Market n/a (n=5) · Right/wrong 4/1\n\n## 🗓️ Next 7 days\n- Oct 28 — Fed decision — hold most likely (about 80%).\n- Oct 29 — Q3 GDP and inflation data — growth ≥1% at 70%.\n- Oct 30 — Brent >$100 (85%), S&P >7,800 (21%).\n- Nov 2–3 — final pre-election polls, Election Day Nov 3.\n\n## 🔭 Timeline (most likely path, framed by Path Gamma)\n- **This week:** oil stays elevated, Fed holds, markets choppy · **This month:** Democrats favored in the House, Senate unresolved; CPI likely hot · **Next 3 months:** December hike risk, Dec 11 funding deadline (shutdown 30%).\n- **What would switch paths:** a US/Israel strike on Iran or a major Gulf infrastructure hit (V toward 0.60+) or, the other way, a verified Iran deal.\n\n## 🆕 New predictions / systems / catalysts\n- None today. Five events scored (Saudi/Houthi attacks, oil/stock close, DOJ pre-election actions, 9th Circuit ballot hearing, Monday oil dip).\n\nNotes: FRED and NPR/BLS feeds were unreachable from the cloud (series marked stale); S&P close from AP's index report, Brent from Reuters/financefeeds, Fed odds from press reports citing CME FedWatch (Oct 20).\n\nSources: [S&P close](https://www.lanacion.com.ar/usa/how-major-us-stock-indexes-fared-friday-10232026-nid23102026/) · [Brent settle](https://financefeeds.com/brent-crude-oil-price-116-72-saturday-week-ahead-houthi-saudi-fed-28-october-bull-120-bear-108/) · [Axios DOJ](https://www.axios.com/2026/10/25/trump-doj-midterms-interference) · ORACLE feed 2026-10-26.\n"};
